BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Songbyrd Music House": "https://dice.fm/event/53lp7l-the-rb-club-discusses-the-legacy-of-janet-jackson-17th-may-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:songbyrd
SUMMARY:The R&B Club Discusses The Legacy of Janet Jackson
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260517T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260517T150000
UID:1660056f5b6df8696823c0a77fa028ab@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:The Jackson family has been in the news a lot lately. For The 
 R&B Club’s next event\, we’re turning the spotlight to Janet Jackson. 
 That’s right. Miss Jackson\, if you’re nasty — or a diehard fan. The
  timing is fitting too given the pop icon’s 60th birthday (May 16) and C
 ontrol turning 40 in February. From Rhythm Nation to the Super Bowl\, we
 ’re playing classics and discussing Janet’s life and times as only we 
 can. One doesn’t just simply like Janet Jackson. One experiences Janet J
 ackson. If she’s soundtracked your life\, we want to hear about it. Rega
 rdless\, come and vibe out with us at Songbyrd in Union Market. It’s the
  last event before Memorial Day unofficially kicks the summer off. You’r
 e going to want to take this playlist with you wherever life takes you ove
 r the next few months. Tickets are $15 in advance and $20 at the door. \\*
 \\*\\* The R&B Club is a cultural gathering founded in 2018 that discusses
  the influence of R&B music. In other words\, think of it as a musical boo
 k club-style meetup. Follow us on social media at @therandbclubdc for more
  information.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/53lp7l-the-rb-club-discusses-the-legacy-of-janet
 -jackson-17th-may-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
