BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Songbyrd Music House": "https://dice.fm/event/7dk5qp-morgan-st-jean-27th-jun-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:songbyrd
SUMMARY:Morgan St. Jean
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260627T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260627T230000
UID:6079e1b679d60490881bdf729a66ad3e@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Morgan St. Jean has been deemed your “favorite up-and-coming
  angsty\, feminist\, socially aware pop princess” — but it’s her ele
 ctric live show that’s turning buzz into a movement. Blending explosive 
 pop production with raw storytelling\, Morgan has quickly built a reputati
 on as a once- in-a-generation performer. In the past few years\, she’s b
 een invited to support four major tours\, including a European run with X 
 Ambassadors. She has performed at SXSW\, LA’s School Night\, and the Lad
 y Gaga x Global Citizen One World: Together At Home concert\, and recently
  completed her debut North American headline tour — solidifying herself 
 as a commanding live force. Beyond the stage\, Morgan is a platinum-sellin
 g songwriter and artist. She co-wrote Chappell Roan’s critically acclaim
 ed single “Casual” (produced by Dan Nigro)\, and her own viral feminis
 t pop anthems — including “Not All Men” and “Do It Like A Girl” 
 — have amassed hundreds of millions of streams while building a fiercely
  loyal global community. With a growing fanbase\, undeniable stage presenc
 e\, and songs that feel both personal and universal\, Morgan St. Jean isn
 ’t just an artist to watch — she’s an artist to experience live. \\*
 \\*\\* Based in New York City\, Chloe Jane is a dance-pop artist\, DJ\, pr
 ofessional figure skater\, and songwriter who has been performing internat
 ionally since age 13. A graduate of the NYU Clive Davis Institute of Recor
 ded Music (Class of 2025)\, she is currently developing her debut album\, 
 Princess of the Night\, a project that reflects her unique artistic identi
 ty as the only emerging artist merging elite-level figure skating with dan
 ce-pop to create a cinematic\, high-energy performance world. Her early ca
 reer included a residency at Amnesia Ibiza and collaborations with artists
  such as Paris Hilton\, helping shape her global\, nightlife-driven sound.
  As a songwriter and collaborator\, Chloe has worked across the electronic
  and pop space\, including releasing “Shut Up” featuring viral duo Fly
 ana Boss\, writing the topline for Layla Benitez’s “Lucid\,” contrib
 uting the topline to Beau Cruz’s “Hero” (Proximity)\, and collaborat
 ing with Grammy-winning duo CamelPhat. Her debut project is supported by a
  seasoned production and songwriting team with credits spanning Ava Max\, 
 David Guetta\, Whitney Houston\, Toni Braxton\, and Jason Derulo.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/7dk5qp-morgan-st-jean-27th-jun-songbyrd-washingt
 on-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
