SUMMARY:Jessie Altman Record Release Show & Benefit for VLA
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260723T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260723T230000
UID:2d223f814b56f0cdda2ed04116af0139@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Jessie Altman is a rising force in music\, named one of SPIN
 ’s “Top Emerging Artists.” With over 1 million streams\, she’s kno
 wn for her cinematic sound and emotionally driven vocals. She is set to re
 turn to the road for a 2026 summer tour as she prepares to release her for
 thcoming second album on September 25\, 2026\, led by the single “Barcel
 ona\,” arriving June 5. Backed by her full band - a phenomenal group of 
 some of Los Angeles' best players - Altman will perform favorites alongsid
 e new music from her album releasing in September\, sharing stories of the
  kind of love that is better than a fairytale. This is a fundraiser for Vo
 lunteer Legal Advocates (VLA) harnessing the power of pro bono advocacy to
  protect survivors of domestic abuse\, uplift children\, and ensure justic
 e is within reach in Washington and Montgomery County\, Maryland. All tick
 et sales will go to VLA and be matched. Band lineup: Guitarist Michael “
 Fish” Herring (Prince\; Stevie Wonder\; Justin Timberlake\; Christina Ag
 uilera\, NKOTB)\, guitarist Mat Dauzat (Seal\, Kelly Osborne)\, bassist La
 rry “Flex” Williams (Christina Aguilera)\, keyboard player Alex Burke 
 (Save Ferris\, Billy Ray Cyrus)\, and drummer Dylan Elise (Blood\, Sweat &
  Tears).
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/k6dlko-jessie-altman-record-release-show-benefit
 -for-vla-23rd-jul-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets
