X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Songbyrd Music House": "https://dice.fm/event/q2v32o-april-vista-fly-on-the-wall-tour-summer-2026-29th-jul-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:songbyrd
SUMMARY:April + VISTA - Fly On The Wall Tour Summer 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260729T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260729T230000
UID:dfc1d02c24eee9a1c82fad78a6f2fa3c@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:April + VISTA is the musical project of the Virginia-raised si
 nger/composer April George and the Maryland-raised composer/producer Matth
 ew Thompson. In a decade-plus of activity\, the duo garnered international
  acclaim with an oeuvre both deeply invested in excavating the impacts of 
 human existence and unbound by the trappings of simple classification. The
 ir first major break came with 2018’s You Are Here\, followed by support
 ing runs with Little Simz\, Little Dragon\, and Mura Masa. Their 2021 foll
 ow-up Pit of My Dreams channeled the duo’s internal and external frustra
 tions into a snapshot of the ripples of burnout\, pushing their experiment
 ation to its roughest and darkest edges. 2023 brought April + VISTA one of
  their biggest crossover moments to date: Slipping Into Color - a collabor
 ative EP with Little Dragon\, made on a trip to Gothenburg\, Sweden - came
  out on the legendary Ninja Tune label. Little Dragon’s 2023 North Ameri
 can and European tours soon followed\, with April + VISTA as direct suppor
 t. April + VISTA’s set to release their debut album Traditional Noise: a
 n exploration of the formative music of their youth\, twisting deeply fami
 liar sounds into strange new territory in an effort to upend the notion of
  popular music. The album’s an exercise in unlocking the feelings and no
 ises of nostalgia to address this life’s persisting anxieties.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/q2v32o-april-vista-fly-on-the-wall-tour-summer-2
 026-29th-jul-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
