BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Songbyrd Music House": "https://dice.fm/event/7dglb6-abby-holiday-charli-adams-7th-aug-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:songbyrd
SUMMARY:Abby Holiday & Charli Adams
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260807T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260807T230000
UID:c80c34385c531c47bcb1d906238bd96d@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Nashville based singer-songwriter\, Abby Holliday\, has been w
 riting songs for as long as she can recall. The 25-year-old burgeoning you
 ng artist is best known for exploring serious themes without taking hersel
 f too seriously. Bearing resemblance to the sonic qualities of female icon
 s Phoebe Bridgers and Japanese House\, Holliday’s songwriting is a uniqu
 e intersection of sad vibes\, introspective lyricism\, and modern pop-sens
 ibility. Holliday attempts to examine her external world as a skeptic — 
 not a cynic — and her internal world with honesty — not cruelty. By wa
 y of the journal entries that she calls her songs\, Holliday invites other
 s to do the very same. \\*\\*\\* Hailing from Alabama\, Charli Adams is a 
 singer-songwriter who found her musical calling at a young age. Leaving hi
 gh school to finish online in a coffee shop\, Adams’ relocated to Nashvi
 lle\, Tennessee at 17 years old. Her makeshift college music history cours
 e was sifting through the dollar CD bin at her local record store\, while 
 immersing herself in the vibrant local scene. Testing out songs and honing
  her craft\, she began recording her debut EP “Good At Being Young”. H
 er first release garnered recognition from none other than Taylor Swift\, 
 who handpicked Charli's self-penned track\, "Backseat\," to be featured on
  her personally curated Women's Day Playlist on Apple Music. This co-sign 
 marked the beginning of Charli's rise in the industry. Charli released her
  critically-acclaimed debut album\, "Bullseye\," which earned high praise 
 from respected publications such as EARMILK\, DORK\, The Fader\, NPR\, Bil
 lboard\, and Line of Best Fit. Collaborations with renowned artists like R
 uston Kelly\, Novo Amor\, and Nightly further solidified her reputation as
  an artist to watch. With an overflowing passion for songwriting\, she has
  also penned songs for artists like Chloe Moriondo\, Yot Club\, Peach Pit\
 , Valley & many more. Charli's musical journey might have started in her b
 edroom\, but on the stage is where her music truly comes alive. With an un
 matched ability to connect with her audience on a personal level\, she qui
 ckly made a name for herself in the Nashville scene and beyond. Whether pe
 rforming with her band or solo\, Charli's undeniable stage presence reveal
 ed that the spotlight is her natural habitat. With a voice that resonates 
 and a sound that captivates\, Charli is an artist poised for greatness\, e
 nchanting hearts with her unique blend of haunting vocals and cinematic st
 orytelling.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/7dglb6-abby-holiday-charli-adams-7th-aug-songbyr
 d-washington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
